  "chain": "Arbitrum One",
  "vulnerability_cn": "ERC-1271 会话授权绕过与验证阶段恶意授权",
  "vulnerability_en": "ERC-1271 session bypass plus validation-phase token approval",
  "detail_cn": "Sodium 的 0x01 签名格式允许 UserOperation 自己填 signer，攻击者用会回传 ERC-1271 magic value 的恶意合约通过签名检查，再让同一地址出现在待建立 sessionKey 中。在未设 safe session 时，代码直接把 isSafe 置真。validateUserOp 随后把攻击者控制的 paymasterAndData 解析成 token 和 spender，调用 approve 给予最大额度。执行阶段被设为零 gas 并失败，但外层 handleOps 成功完成，验证阶段的授权因此保留；后续 transferFrom 取走账户代币。Sourcify 对 Sodium 实现给出 creation/runtime exact match。",
  "detail_en": "Sodium's type-0x01 signature lets the UserOperation choose its signer. A malicious ERC-1271 contract returned the magic value, while the same attacker-controlled address was supplied as the proposed session key; with no safe session configured, isSafe was true. validateUserOp then parsed attacker-controlled paymasterAndData into a token and spender and approved the maximum allowance. Account execution used zero gas and failed, but handleOps completed, leaving the validation-phase allowance persistent for a later transferFrom drain. Sourcify reports exact creation/runtime match for the Sodium implementation.",
  "tx_urls": [
    "https://arbiscan.io/tx/0x020995ec0b5daafe8fab481e33b1b52fdbd6423578060a1f73fd2a9b9fb0ea90"
  ],
